From 1e227491dda18f2c0a769488410f5a4e6a207d8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:01:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bundle numpy and scipy into the fuzz targets explicitly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every ClusterFuzzLite target failed its bad-build check with
`No module named 'numpy._core._exceptions'`. No fuzzer ran; the frozen
executables died on `import otwin`.

PyInstaller decides what to bundle by static analysis plus a per-package hook.
OSS-Fuzz's base-builder pins PyInstaller 5.0.1 (April 2022). numpy 2.0 moved
its implementation from `numpy.core` to `numpy._core` and imports it
dynamically, so that hook collects a module layout that no longer exists.

build.sh installs the package with `pip install .` and pyproject declares
`numpy>=1.24`, so the fuzz image resolves numpy to whatever is newest on PyPI
that day — 2.4.6 in the failing run. The build was never reproducible and broke
on a day nothing in the repository changed.

`--collect-all` walks the installed package instead of trusting the hook.
scipy is included for the same exposure, not because it has failed yet: it is
imported by the same path and fails second, which would cost another CI round
trip to discover.
---
 .clusterfuzzlite/build.sh | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.clusterfuzzlite/build.sh b/.clusterfuzzlite/build.sh
index 66badf0..9e1e3cd 100755
--- a/.clusterfuzzlite/build.sh
+++ b/.clusterfuzzlite/build.sh
@@ -13,9 +13,18 @@ python3 -m pip install .
 # four bytes of the discovery routine.
 python3 fuzz/make_seed_corpus.py "$WORK/corpus"
 
+# --collect-all is not optional. PyInstaller freezes each target into one
+# executable and decides what to bundle by static analysis plus per-package
+# hooks. OSS-Fuzz's base-builder pins PyInstaller 5.0.1 (April 2022); numpy 2.0
+# moved its implementation from numpy.core to numpy._core and imports it
+# dynamically, so the 2022 hook collects a set of modules that no longer exists
+# and the frozen target dies on `import numpy` with
+# `No module named 'numpy._core._exceptions'`. --collect-all walks the installed
+# package instead of trusting the hook. scipy is listed for the same reason and
+# not because it has failed yet.
 for target in fuzz/fuzz_*.py; do
   name=$(basename "$target" .py)
-  compile_python_fuzzer "$target"
+  compile_python_fuzzer "$target" --collect-all numpy --collect-all scipy
 
   case "$name" in
     fuzz_sunspec_chain) seed="$WORK/corpus/sunspec_chain" ;;
-- 
2.43.0

